(function (l, F, LB, T) { const N = window.AtlasNews = window.AtlasNews || { FACTS: {}, LABEL: {}, TAGS: {}, has: {} }; N.has = N.has || {};
  Object.keys(F).forEach(k => { (N.FACTS[k] = N.FACTS[k] || {})[l] = F[k]; }); N.LABEL[l] = LB; Object.keys(T).forEach(k => { (N.TAGS[k] = N.TAGS[k] || {})[l] = T[k]; }); N.has[l] = 1;
})("en", {"01-01":"On this day in 1983, ARPANET switched over to TCP/IP — often called the birthday of today's internet.","01-02":"Today is kakizome in Japan: the year's first calligraphy, when people brush a wish or lucky word for the new year.","01-03":"On this day in 1892, J. R. R. Tolkien, author of The Hobbit and The Lord of the Rings, was born in Bloemfontein, South Africa.","01-04":"It's World Braille Day, the birthday of Louis Braille, the Frenchman who invented braille, born on this day in 1809.","01-05":"It's Go Day in Japan: 1-5 can be read i-go, so the Nihon Ki-in made it a day for the game of Go.","01-06":"On this day in 1912, Alfred Wegener first presented his idea that the continents drift — continental drift.","01-07":"In Japan, January 7 is for nanakusa-gayu: rice porridge with seven spring herbs, eaten for good health in the new year.","01-08":"On this day in 1942, physicist Stephen Hawking was born in Oxford — exactly 300 years after Galileo died.","01-09":"On this day in 2007, Steve Jobs unveiled the first iPhone at Macworld in San Francisco.","01-10":"On this day in 1863, the world's first underground railway opened in London, running steam trains from Paddington to Farringdon.","01-11":"It's kagami biraki in Japan: the New Year's kagami mochi rice cakes are broken open and eaten, often in sweet red-bean soup.","01-12":"On this day in 1628, Charles Perrault, whose fairy tales include Cinderella and Puss in Boots, was born in Paris.","01-13":"On this day in 1910, opera with Enrico Caruso was broadcast live from New York's Metropolitan Opera — the first public radio broadcast.","01-14":"On this day in 1959, Taro and Jiro — two Sakhalin huskies left behind in Antarctica for a year — were found alive at Showa Station.","01-15":"On this day in 2001, Wikipedia — the free encyclopedia anyone can edit — went online.","01-16":"On this day in 1605, the first part of Cervantes's Don Quixote was published in Madrid — often called the first modern novel.","01-17":"On this day in 1706, Benjamin Franklin — inventor of the lightning rod and bifocal glasses — was born in Boston.","01-18":"It's Winnie-the-Pooh Day! A. A. Milne, the bear's creator, was born in London on this day in 1882.","01-19":"On this day in 1736, James Watt, who greatly improved the steam engine, was born in Scotland. The unit \"watt\" is named after him.","01-20":"On this day in 1920, Italian film director Federico Fellini, known for La Strada and La Dolce Vita, was born in Rimini.","01-21":"On this day in 1976, Concorde began passenger service, with flights taking off at the same time from London to Bahrain and Paris to Rio.","01-22":"It's Curry Day in Japan: on this day in 1982, schools across the country all served curry for lunch.","01-23":"On this day in 1907, physicist Hideki Yukawa was born. His meson theory made him Japan's first Nobel laureate in 1949.","01-24":"On this day in 1848, James Marshall found gold at Sutter's Mill in California — the start of the Gold Rush.","01-25":"On this day in 1902, Asahikawa in Hokkaido hit −41.0 °C — still Japan's official record low.","01-26":"On this day in 1905, the 3,106-carat Cullinan was found in a South African mine — the largest gem diamond ever discovered.","01-27":"On this day in 1756, composer Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born in Salzburg, Austria.","01-28":"On this day in 1958, at 1:58 pm, the LEGO brick in its modern form was submitted for a patent in Denmark.","01-29":"On this day in 1957, Japan's first Antarctic expedition landed on East Ongul Island and opened Showa Station.","01-30":"On this day in 1969, the Beatles played a surprise concert on a London rooftop — their last public performance.","01-31":"On this day in 1797, Franz Schubert, the \"king of song\", was born in Vienna. He wrote more than 600 songs.","02-01":"On this day in 1953, NHK began Japan's first regular television broadcasts in Tokyo.","02-02":"It's Groundhog Day! If the groundhog sees its shadow, six more weeks of winter — a US tradition since 1887.","02-03":"On this day in 1809, Felix Mendelssohn, composer of the famous Wedding March, was born in Hamburg.","02-04":"On this day in 2004, \"TheFacebook\" went live from a Harvard dorm room — the site that became Facebook.","02-05":"On this day in 1840, John Boyd Dunlop was born in Scotland. He made the first practical air-filled tyre — for his son's tricycle.","02-06":"It's Nori Day in Japan: the Taihō Code of 701 listed nori seaweed as a product to be paid as tax.","02-07":"On this day in 1867, Laura Ingalls Wilder, author of the Little House on the Prairie books, was born in Wisconsin.","02-08":"On this day in 1828, Jules Verne, author of Around the World in Eighty Days and Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas, was born in Nantes.","02-09":"On this day in 1895, William G. Morgan in Massachusetts invented a new game called \"Mintonette\" — today's volleyball.","02-10":"On this day in 1996, IBM's Deep Blue beat world chess champion Garry Kasparov in Game 1 — the first computer win over a reigning champion under standard rules.","02-11":"It's the UN International Day of Women and Girls in Science, set in 2015 to champion women and girls in science.","02-12":"On this day in 1924, Gershwin's Rhapsody in Blue premiered in New York, opening with its famous clarinet glissando.","02-13":"On this day in 1875, Japan required everyone to have a family name — many commoners chose a surname for the first time.","02-14":"On this day in 1990, Voyager 1 photographed Earth from about 6 billion km away — the tiny speck known as the \"Pale Blue Dot\".","02-15":"On this day in 1564, Galileo Galilei, who used a telescope to discover Jupiter's moons, was born in Pisa, Italy.","02-16":"On this day in 1883, Japan's first weather map was drawn, using telegrams from 11 weather stations across the country.","02-17":"On this day in 1904, Puccini's opera Madama Butterfly, set in Nagasaki, premiered at La Scala in Milan.","02-18":"On this day in 1930, Clyde Tombaugh discovered Pluto at Lowell Observatory in Arizona.","02-19":"On this day in 1473, Nicolaus Copernicus, who argued that Earth goes around the Sun, was born in Toruń, Poland.","02-20":"On this day in 1962, John Glenn circled Earth three times in Friendship 7 — the first American to orbit the planet.","02-21":"It's International Mother Language Day, proclaimed by UNESCO in 1999 to celebrate the world's many languages.","02-22":"It's Cat Day in Japan: 2-2-2 sounds like nyan nyan nyan, \"meow meow meow\" — set in 1987.","02-23":"It's Mount Fuji Day: 2-2-3 can be read fu-ji-san. Yamanashi and Shizuoka mark it, and the clear winter air shows the peak at its best.","02-24":"On this day in 1786, Wilhelm Grimm was born in Hanau, Germany. With his brother Jacob, he collected Grimm's Fairy Tales.","02-25":"On this day in 1841, Impressionist painter Pierre-Auguste Renoir was born in Limoges, France.","02-26":"On this day in 1802, Victor Hugo, author of Les Misérables and The Hunchback of Notre-Dame, was born in Besançon, France.","02-27":"It's Pokémon Day! On this day in 1996, Pocket Monsters Red and Green came out for the Game Boy in Japan.","02-28":"On this day in 1953, Watson and Crick worked out DNA's double helix. Crick reportedly told a Cambridge pub they'd found \"the secret of life\".","02-29":"It's leap day! On February 29, 1792, Gioachino Rossini, composer of The Barber of Seville, was born in Pesaro, Italy.","03-01":"On this day in 1872, Yellowstone in the US became the world's first national park, famous for its geysers and hot springs.","03-02":"On this day in 1904, Dr. Seuss, author of The Cat in the Hat, was born in Massachusetts. His birthday is Read Across America Day.","03-03":"It's Hinamatsuri, Japan's Doll Festival: families display hina dolls and wish for their daughters' health and happiness.","03-04":"On this day in 1678, Antonio Vivaldi, composer of The Four Seasons, was born in Venice.","03-05":"On this day in 1512, mapmaker Gerardus Mercator, creator of the still-used Mercator projection, was born in Flanders.","03-06":"On this day in 1475, Michelangelo — sculptor of David and painter of the Sistine Chapel ceiling — was born in Caprese, Italy.","03-07":"On this day in 1875, Maurice Ravel, composer of Boléro, was born in Ciboure in southwest France.","03-08":"It's International Women's Day, marked by the UN since 1975. In Italy, people give sprigs of yellow mimosa.","03-09":"On this day in 1959, the Barbie doll made her debut at the American International Toy Fair in New York.","03-10":"On this day in 1876, Alexander Graham Bell made the first telephone call: \"Mr. Watson, come here — I want to see you.\"","03-11":"On this day in 1811, French astronomer Urbain Le Verrier was born — he predicted where Neptune was using only mathematics.","03-12":"On this day in 1912, Juliette Gordon Low formed the first Girl Scout troop in Savannah, Georgia.","03-13":"On this day in 1781, William Herschel discovered Uranus with a homemade telescope — the first planet found by telescope.","03-14":"Happy Pi Day! 3/14 for 3.14 — started in 1988 at San Francisco's Exploratorium. It's also Einstein's birthday.","03-15":"It's Shoe Day in Japan: on this day in 1870, Nishimura Katsuzō opened the country's first Western-style shoe factory in Tokyo.","03-16":"On this day in 1926, Robert Goddard launched the world's first liquid-fuelled rocket. The flight lasted just 2.5 seconds.","03-17":"On this day in 1834, car pioneer Gottlieb Daimler was born in Schorndorf, Germany. He developed a small, fast-running petrol engine.","03-18":"On this day in 1965, Alexei Leonov stepped outside Voskhod 2 and made the first spacewalk in history.","03-19":"On this day in 1932, the Sydney Harbour Bridge opened. Locals still call it \"the Coathanger\".","03-20":"It's the UN International Day of Happiness, created in 2012 and celebrated since 2013.","03-21":"On this day in 1685, Johann Sebastian Bach, often called the father of music, was born in Eisenach, Germany.","03-22":"It's World Water Day, a UN day held since 1993 to think about the value of clean water.","03-23":"It's World Meteorological Day, marking the day in 1950 when the World Meteorological Organization's convention came into force.","03-24":"On this day in 1882, Robert Koch announced he had discovered the bacterium that causes tuberculosis. It's now World TB Day.","03-25":"It's Electricity Day in Japan: on this day in 1878, arc lamps lit up a Tokyo college hall — the country's first electric light.","03-26":"On this day in 1874, poet Robert Frost was born in San Francisco. He won four Pulitzer Prizes and wrote \"The Road Not Taken\".","03-27":"It's Cherry Blossom Day in Japan: sa (3) × ku (9) = 27, a sakura pun chosen in 1992 by the Japan Cherry Blossom Association.","03-28":"It's Mitsuya Cider Day in Japan: 3-2-8 reads mi-tsu-ya, after the fizzy drink sold since the 1880s.","03-29":"On this day in 1974, NASA's Mariner 10 flew past Mercury — the first spacecraft ever to visit the planet.","03-30":"On this day in 1853, Vincent van Gogh, painter of Sunflowers and The Starry Night, was born in Zundert, the Netherlands.","03-31":"On this day in 1889, the Eiffel Tower was completed and Gustave Eiffel raised a flag at the top. At 300 m, it was the world's tallest structure.","04-01":"On this day in 1976, Steve Jobs and Steve Wozniak, with Ronald Wayne, founded Apple Computer.","04-02":"It's International Children's Book Day, held on the birthday of Hans Christian Andersen, born on this day in 1805.","04-03":"On this day in 1973, Motorola's Martin Cooper made the first handheld cellphone call on a New York street.","04-04":"It's Anpan Day in Japan: on this day in 1875, Kimuraya's sweet bean bun with a salted cherry blossom was presented to Emperor Meiji.","04-05":"Joseph Lister was born on this day in 1827. The British surgeon pioneered antiseptic surgery, making operations far safer.","04-06":"On this day in 1896, the first modern Olympic Games opened in Athens, Greece.","04-07":"It's World Health Day, marking the founding of the World Health Organization (WHO) on this day in 1948.","04-08":"On this day in 1911, Heike Kamerlingh Onnes saw the electrical resistance of ultra-cold mercury vanish — the discovery of superconductivity.","04-09":"On this day in 1860, Édouard-Léon Scott de Martinville recorded \"Au clair de la lune\". Played back in 2008, it's the oldest known recording of a human voice.","04-10":"On this day in 1849, American inventor Walter Hunt received a patent for the safety pin.","04-11":"On this day in 1921, Japan promulgated a revised Weights and Measures Act that adopted the metric system.","04-12":"On this day in 1961, Yuri Gagarin orbited Earth once aboard Vostok 1 — the first human spaceflight, lasting about 108 minutes.","04-13":"Alfred Mosher Butts, the American architect who invented the word game Scrabble, was born on this day in 1899.","04-14":"Christiaan Huygens was born on this day in 1629. The Dutch scientist invented the pendulum clock and explained Saturn's rings.","04-15":"Leonardo da Vinci was born on this day in 1452 near Vinci, Tuscany — painter, inventor and endlessly curious mind.","04-16":"Charlie Chaplin was born on this day in 1889 in London. His bowler-hatted Little Tramp made the whole world laugh.","04-17":"On this day in 1964, the Ford Mustang was unveiled at the New York World's Fair.","04-18":"It's Invention Day in Japan: on this day in 1885, the country's first patent law was promulgated.","04-19":"It's Map Day in Japan: on this day in 1800 (old calendar), Ino Tadataka left Edo to survey Ezo, starting his journey to map all of Japan.","04-20":"It's Postal Day in Japan: on this day in 1871, a modern mail service proposed by Maejima Hisoka began between Tokyo and Osaka.","04-21":"Friedrich Fröbel was born on this day in 1782. The German educator created the kindergarten — the \"children's garden\".","04-22":"It's Earth Day, first held on this day in 1970, when about 20 million Americans took part.","04-23":"It's World Book and Copyright Day, proclaimed by UNESCO in 1995 to celebrate books and reading.","04-24":"On this day in 1990, Space Shuttle Discovery lifted off carrying the Hubble Space Telescope.","04-25":"On this day in 1953, Watson and Crick's paper describing DNA's double helix was published in the journal Nature.","04-26":"It's World Intellectual Property Day: the convention creating WIPO came into force on this day in 1970.","04-27":"Samuel Morse was born on this day in 1791. A painter first, he went on to develop the telegraph and Morse code.","04-28":"On this day in 1947, Thor Heyerdahl's balsa raft Kon-Tiki set sail from Peru. It reached Polynesia 101 days later.","04-29":"On this day in 1973, Othello, the board game devised by Goro Hasegawa, went on sale across Japan from Tsukuda.","04-30":"Carl Friedrich Gauss was born on this day in 1777 in Brunswick. He's often called the \"prince of mathematicians\".","05-01":"On this day in 1931, New York's Empire State Building opened. It stayed the world's tallest building for nearly 40 years.","05-02":"On this day in 1952, a BOAC de Havilland Comet flew from London to Johannesburg — the world's first scheduled jet airliner service.","05-03":"On this day in 1952, a ski-equipped U.S. C-47 flown by Joseph Fletcher and William Benedict became the first plane to land at the North Pole.","05-04":"Audrey Hepburn was born on this day in 1929 in Brussels. \"Roman Holiday\" made her a star loved worldwide.","05-05":"It's Children's Day in Japan, a national holiday since 1948. Carp streamers called koinobori fly in the sky.","05-06":"On this day in 1840, the Penny Black — the world's first adhesive postage stamp — became valid for use in Britain.","05-07":"Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was born on this day in 1840 — the composer of \"Swan Lake\" and \"The Nutcracker\".","05-08":"It's World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, the birthday of founder Henry Dunant, born on this day in 1828.","05-09":"It's Ice Cream Day in Japan. The country's first ice cream, called \"aisukurin\", was sold in Yokohama in 1869.","05-10":"On this day in 1869, the golden spike was driven at Promontory Summit, Utah, completing America's first transcontinental railroad.","05-11":"On this day in 1997, IBM's Deep Blue won its six-game match against world chess champion Garry Kasparov.","05-12":"It's International Nurses Day, the birthday of Florence Nightingale, the founder of modern nursing, born on this day in 1820.","05-13":"It's Cocktail Day in Japan: on this day in 1806, an American magazine first printed a definition of the word \"cocktail\".","05-14":"On this day in 1796, Edward Jenner inoculated young James Phipps with cowpox — the first vaccine, against smallpox.","05-15":"On this day in 1940, nylon stockings went on sale across the United States, and shoppers lined up to get them.","05-16":"It's Travel Day in Japan: on this day in 1689, the haiku poet Matsuo Basho left Edo on the journey of \"The Narrow Road to the Deep North\".","05-17":"It's World Telecommunication Day: on this day in 1865, the International Telegraph Union — today's ITU — was founded in Paris.","05-18":"It's International Museum Day, celebrated by museums around the world since ICOM started it in 1977.","05-19":"It's Boxing Day in Japan: on this day in 1952, Yoshio Shirai won the world flyweight title, becoming Japan's first boxing world champion.","05-20":"On this day in 1873, Levi Strauss and Jacob Davis patented riveted work pants — the birth of blue jeans.","05-21":"On this day in 1927, Charles Lindbergh landed the Spirit of St. Louis in Paris after 33.5 hours — the first solo nonstop flight across the Atlantic.","05-22":"On this day in 1980, Namco's arcade game Pac-Man, created by Toru Iwatani, debuted in Japan.","05-23":"Carl Linnaeus was born on this day in 1707 in Sweden. He popularized two-part scientific names like \"Homo sapiens\".","05-24":"On this day in 1883, New York's Brooklyn Bridge opened — at the time, the longest suspension bridge in the world.","05-25":"On this day in 1977, \"Star Wars\" opened in American theaters.","05-26":"On this day in 1897, Bram Stoker's novel \"Dracula\" was published in London — it's World Dracula Day.","05-27":"On this day in 1937, San Francisco's Golden Gate Bridge opened, and about 200,000 people walked across on the first day.","05-28":"It's Fireworks Day in Japan: on this day in 1733, fireworks lit up Edo's Ryogoku river festival — the roots of today's Sumida River Fireworks.","05-29":"On this day in 1953, Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay became the first to stand on the summit of Mount Everest.","05-30":"On this day in 1911, the first Indianapolis 500 was held, won by Ray Harroun in the Marmon Wasp.","05-31":"On this day in 1859, the Great Clock of Westminster — \"Big Ben\" — began keeping time over London.","06-01":"It's Meteorology Day in Japan: on this day in 1875, the Tokyo Meteorological Observatory began weather observations.","06-02":"It's Yokohama Port Opening Day: the Port of Yokohama opened to foreign trade on this date in 1859.","06-03":"On this day in 1965, Ed White of Gemini 4 became the first American to walk in space.","06-04":"It's Cavity Prevention Day in Japan, started in 1928 by the Japan Dental Association — \"6-4\" can be read \"mushi\", as in mushiba (cavity).","06-05":"It's World Environment Day, held since 1974 to mark the opening of the UN Stockholm Conference on the Human Environment on this day in 1972.","06-06":"On this day in 1984, Alexey Pajitnov's falling-block puzzle Tetris was born in Moscow.","06-07":"Paul Gauguin was born on this day in 1848 in Paris. He painted Tahiti in bold, glowing colors.","06-08":"It's World Oceans Day, officially observed by the United Nations since 2009 to celebrate and protect the sea.","06-09":"George Stephenson was born on this day in 1781. The English engineer is known as the \"Father of Railways\".","06-10":"It's Time Day in Japan, set in 1920 to remember how Emperor Tenji's water clock first sounded the hours in 671.","06-11":"Jacques-Yves Cousteau was born on this day in 1910. The French ocean explorer co-developed the Aqua-Lung diving gear.","06-12":"On this day in 1939, the National Baseball Hall of Fame and Museum opened in Cooperstown, New York.","06-13":"On this day in 1983, Pioneer 10 crossed Neptune's orbit — the first human-made object to travel beyond the planets.","06-14":"It's World Blood Donor Day, on the birthday of Karl Landsteiner, discoverer of the ABO blood groups, born on this day in 1868.","06-15":"Edvard Grieg was born on this day in 1843 in Bergen, Norway. His \"In the Hall of the Mountain King\" from \"Peer Gynt\" is world-famous.","06-16":"It's Wagashi Day in Japan, set in 1979 after the old Kajo custom — said to date back to 848 — of eating sweets for good health.","06-17":"M. C. Escher was born on this day in 1898 in the Netherlands, the artist of impossible staircases and mind-bending tilings.","06-18":"On this day in 1908, the Kasato Maru reached Santos, Brazil, with 781 Japanese emigrants — the start of Japanese immigration to Brazil.","06-19":"Blaise Pascal was born on this day in 1623. He built a calculating machine and, puzzling over games of chance, helped found probability theory.","06-20":"On this day in 1975, Steven Spielberg's \"Jaws\" opened in the U.S. — often called the first summer blockbuster.","06-21":"It's the Fête de la Musique, the midsummer music festival that began in France in 1982 and now fills streets worldwide with music.","06-22":"On this day in 1675, King Charles II founded the Royal Observatory in Greenwich — later home of the prime meridian, 0° longitude.","06-23":"Alan Turing was born on this day in 1912 in London. The mathematician laid the foundations of computer science and AI.","06-24":"On this day in 1947, pilot Kenneth Arnold reported strange objects near Mount Rainier — and the term \"flying saucer\" took off.","06-25":"Antoni Gaudí was born on this day in 1852 in Catalonia, Spain — the architect of the Sagrada Família.","06-26":"On this day in 1997, \"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone\" was published in the UK. The first hardback printing was just 500 copies.","06-27":"Helen Keller was born on this day in 1880 in Tuscumbia, Alabama. Deaf and blind from early childhood, she became an author and activist.","06-28":"Peter Paul Rubens, the great Baroque painter, was born on this day in 1577 in Siegen.","06-29":"Antoine de Saint-Exupéry was born on this day in 1900 in Lyon — aviator and author of \"The Little Prince\".","06-30":"It's International Asteroid Day, proclaimed by the UN in 2016 on the anniversary of the 1908 Tunguska blast over Siberia.","07-01":"On this day in 1979, Sony released the first Walkman, the TPS-L2. Music became something you could carry.","07-02":"On this day in 1698, Thomas Savery patented his steam pump for \"raising water by fire\" — an early steam engine.","07-03":"On this day in 1938, the British steam locomotive Mallard hit 126 mph (203 km/h) — a steam record that still stands.","07-04":"On this day in 2012, CERN announced the discovery of a new particle consistent with the Higgs boson — the one that gives matter its mass.","07-05":"On this day in 1996, Dolly the sheep was born — the first mammal cloned from an adult cell.","07-06":"On this day in 1885, Louis Pasteur first gave his rabies vaccine to a person — young Joseph Meister, who recovered.","07-07":"Tanabata, Japan's star festival: the night Orihime and Hikoboshi meet across the Milky Way. People hang wishes on bamboo.","07-08":"Ferdinand von Zeppelin, father of the rigid airship, was born on this day in 1838 in Konstanz, Germany.","07-09":"Japan's \"Roller Coaster Day\": Tokyo's Korakuen amusement park opened on this day in 1955 with the country's first full-scale roller coaster.","07-10":"Nikola Tesla, the inventor behind AC power and the induction motor, was born on this day in 1856.","07-11":"World Population Day (UN). It marks 11 July 1987, when the world's population was estimated to reach 5 billion.","07-12":"Japan's \"Radio Broadcasting Day\": on this day in 1925, Tokyo Broadcasting Station began Japan's first regular radio service from Mount Atago.","07-13":"Ernő Rubik, who invented the Rubik's Cube, was born on this day in 1944 in Budapest.","07-14":"Gustav Klimt, the Austrian painter of the gold-leaf masterpiece \"The Kiss\", was born on this day in 1862.","07-15":"On this day in 1983, Nintendo released the Family Computer (Famicom) in Japan for ¥14,800.","07-16":"On this day in 1935, the world's first parking meter was installed in Oklahoma City, USA.","07-17":"Disneyland opened on this day in 1955 in Anaheim, California.","07-18":"On this day in 1968, Robert Noyce and Gordon Moore founded the chipmaker Intel.","07-19":"On this day in 1843, Brunel's SS Great Britain was launched in Bristol — a pioneering steamship with an iron hull and a screw propeller.","07-20":"On this day in 1969, Apollo 11's lunar module Eagle landed on the Moon, and Neil Armstrong took humanity's first step there.","07-21":"On this day in 1983, Vostok Station in Antarctica recorded −89.2 °C — the lowest air temperature ever measured on the ground.","07-22":"On this day in 2009, a total solar eclipse was seen from Japan's Tokara Islands — the first on Japanese land in 46 years.","07-23":"Japan's \"Letter Day\": July's old name fumizuki and the pun fu-mi (2-3) mean \"letter\" — a day to enjoy writing one.","07-24":"On this day in 1911, explorer Hiram Bingham reached Machu Picchu in Peru and made the Inca city known to the wider world.","07-25":"Japan's \"Shaved Ice Day\": 7-2-5 reads as natsu-gōri (\"summer ice\"), and Yamagata hit 40.8 °C on this day in 1933.","07-26":"Esperanto Day: on this day in 1887, Zamenhof published the first textbook of the international language Esperanto.","07-27":"On this day in 1940, the cartoon \"A Wild Hare\" came out — Bugs Bunny's official debut, and the first \"What's up, Doc?\"","07-28":"Beatrix Potter, author of \"The Tale of Peter Rabbit\", was born on this day in 1866 in London.","07-29":"On this day in 1958, the National Aeronautics and Space Act was signed in the US, creating NASA.","07-30":"Emily Brontë, author of \"Wuthering Heights\", was born on this day in 1818 in Yorkshire, England.","07-31":"On this day in 1790, the first U.S. patent was issued — to Samuel Hopkins, for a new way of making potash.","08-01":"On this day in 1774, Joseph Priestley isolated oxygen — a key moment in modern chemistry.","08-02":"On this day in 1932, Carl Anderson photographed a positron track in a cloud chamber — the first antimatter ever found.","08-03":"Japan's \"Honey Day\": 8-3 can be read hachi-mitsu, the Japanese word for honey.","08-04":"Jazz trumpeter and singer Louis Armstrong was born on this day in 1901 in New Orleans.","08-05":"On this day in 1888, Bertha Benz drove her husband's motor car about 100 km from Mannheim to Pforzheim — the first long-distance car trip.","08-06":"On this day in 1991, Tim Berners-Lee posted the World Wide Web project publicly online, opening it up to everyone.","08-07":"Japan's \"Banana Day\": 8-7 can be read ba-na(na), so Japan's banana importers' association picked this date.","08-08":"International Cat Day, started in 2002 by the International Fund for Animal Welfare (IFAW) — a day to celebrate cats.","08-09":"Moomin Day: Tove Jansson, the Finnish creator of the Moomins, was born on this day in 1914.","08-10":"On this day in 1846, the Smithsonian Institution was founded \"for the increase and diffusion of knowledge\". It is now one of the world's largest museum groups.","08-11":"Mountain Day, a Japanese national holiday since 2016 — a day to enjoy the mountains and be grateful for them.","08-12":"On this day in 1981, IBM announced the IBM Personal Computer (model 5150), the ancestor of today's PCs.","08-13":"John Logie Baird, the Scottish pioneer who first transmitted moving television images, was born on this day in 1888.","08-14":"Hans Christian Ørsted, the Danish physicist who found that electric current moves a compass needle, was born on this day in 1777.","08-15":"On this day in 1914, the Panama Canal opened as the SS Ancon made the first official transit between the Atlantic and the Pacific.","08-16":"On this day in 1896, gold was found on Bonanza Creek in Canada's Yukon, setting off the Klondike Gold Rush.","08-17":"On this day in 1978, the balloon Double Eagle II landed in France — the first balloon ever to cross the Atlantic.","08-18":"Japan's High School Baseball Day: the first national tournament, forerunner of summer Koshien, opened on this day in 1915 in Toyonaka, Osaka.","08-19":"World Photography Day: on this day in 1839, France made Daguerre's photographic process public as a gift \"free to the world\".","08-20":"On this day in 1977, Voyager 2 was launched. It is still the only spacecraft to have visited Uranus and Neptune.","08-21":"Jazz pianist and big-band leader Count Basie was born on this day in 1904 in Red Bank, New Jersey.","08-22":"French composer Claude Debussy, known for \"Clair de lune\", was born on this day in 1862 near Paris.","08-23":"On this day in 1966, NASA's Lunar Orbiter 1 took the first photo of Earth as seen from near the Moon.","08-24":"On this day in 2006, the International Astronomical Union defined \"planet\", and Pluto was reclassified as a dwarf planet.","08-25":"Instant Ramen Day in Japan: Momofuku Ando's Chicken Ramen, the world's first instant ramen, went on sale on this day in 1958.","08-26":"French chemist Antoine Lavoisier, often called the father of modern chemistry, was born on this day in 1743 in Paris.","08-27":"In Japan, it's \"Otoko wa Tsurai yo\" Day: the first Tora-san film opened on this day in 1969, and the series ran to 48 films by 1995.","08-28":"TV Commercial Day in Japan: on this day in 1953, Nippon TV began broadcasting and aired Japan's first TV ad — a Seikosha clock's noon time signal.","08-29":"Japan's Yakiniku Day: 8-2-9 can be read ya-ki-niku, \"grilled meat\". The day was set in 1993 by the national yakiniku association.","08-30":"Physicist Ernest Rutherford, who discovered the atomic nucleus, was born on this day in 1871 in New Zealand.","08-31":"Japan's Vegetable Day: 8-3-1 can be read ya-sa-i, \"vegetables\". Produce trade groups set it up in 1983.","09-01":"On this day in 1878, Emma Nutt started work in Boston as the world's first woman telephone operator.","09-02":"On this day in 1969, America's first ATM began dispensing cash at a Chemical Bank branch in Rockville Centre, New York.","09-03":"Doraemon's birthday! The robot cat from the future is said to be born on 3 September 2112.","09-04":"On this day in 1882, Edison's Pearl Street Station began supplying power in New York — the start of commercial central power stations.","09-05":"Queen's lead singer Freddie Mercury was born on this day in 1946 in Zanzibar.","09-06":"English chemist John Dalton, pioneer of modern atomic theory, was born on this day in 1766.","09-07":"CM Song Day in Japan: on this day in 1951, Japan's first commercial jingle, Miki Toriro's \"Boku wa Amateur Cameraman\", aired on radio.","09-08":"International Literacy Day, proclaimed by UNESCO in 1966 to celebrate the power of reading and writing.","09-09":"On this day in 1947, a moth was found stuck in a relay of Harvard's Mark II computer and logged as the \"first actual case of bug being found\".","09-10":"On this day in 1846, American inventor Elias Howe received a patent for his lockstitch sewing machine.","09-11":"Public Telephone Day in Japan: the country's first public phones were installed at Tokyo's Shimbashi and Ueno stations on this day in 1900.","09-12":"On this day in 1940, four teenagers in France crawled into the Lascaux cave and found its stunning prehistoric paintings.","09-13":"Roald Dahl, author of \"Charlie and the Chocolate Factory\", was born on this day in 1916 in Wales.","09-14":"On this day in 1959, the Soviet probe Luna 2 reached the Moon — the first human-made object to touch another world.","09-15":"Agatha Christie, the \"Queen of Crime\" who created Poirot and Miss Marple, was born on this day in 1890 in Torquay, England.","09-16":"International Day for the Preservation of the Ozone Layer, marking the signing of the Montreal Protocol on this day in 1987.","09-17":"On this day in 1991, Linus Torvalds put the very first version of Linux, 0.01, online.","09-18":"French physicist Léon Foucault, who used a pendulum to show the Earth's rotation, was born on this day in 1819.","09-19":"On this day in 1982, Scott Fahlman at Carnegie Mellon proposed :-) to mark jokes online — the first smiley emoticon.","09-20":"Sky Day in Japan: on this day in 1911, Yamada Isaburo's airship completed a flight circling the skies over Tokyo.","09-21":"H. G. Wells, author of \"The Time Machine\" and \"The War of the Worlds\", was born on this day in 1866 in England.","09-22":"Michael Faraday, the scientist who discovered electromagnetic induction, was born on this day in 1791 in London.","09-23":"On this day in 1889, Fusajiro Yamauchi founded Nintendo in Kyoto — as a maker of handmade hanafuda playing cards.","09-24":"Jim Henson, the puppeteer who created the Muppets and Kermit the Frog, was born on this day in 1936 in Mississippi.","09-25":"Composer Dmitri Shostakovich, who wrote 15 symphonies, was born on this day in 1906 in St Petersburg.","09-26":"On this day in 1957, Leonard Bernstein's musical \"West Side Story\" opened on Broadway.","09-27":"World Tourism Day, observed since 1980 — a UN day to celebrate how travel connects people and cultures.","09-28":"On this day in 1928, Alexander Fleming noticed a mould in a petri dish — the start of the discovery of penicillin.","09-29":"Maneki-neko Day in Japan: 9-2-9 can be read ku-ru-fuku, \"good fortune comes\" — perfect for the beckoning cat.","09-30":"On this day in 1791, Mozart's opera \"The Magic Flute\" premiered in Vienna.","10-01":"On this day in 1964, the Tokaido Shinkansen opened, linking Tokyo and Shin-Osaka in four hours — the world's first high-speed railway.","10-02":"On this day in 1950, Charles M. Schulz's comic strip \"Peanuts\" debuted in seven newspapers. Snoopy appeared soon after.","10-03":"Japan's Mountain Climbing Day: 10-3 can be read to-zan, \"climbing\", and the Japanese Alpine Club was founded in October 1905.","10-04":"On this day in 1957, the Soviet Union launched Sputnik 1, the first artificial satellite — the dawn of the space age.","10-05":"World Teachers' Day, held since 1994 on the anniversary of the 1966 UNESCO/ILO Recommendation on the Status of Teachers.","10-06":"On this day in 1927, \"The Jazz Singer\" premiered in New York — the first feature-length film with spoken dialogue.","10-07":"Physicist Niels Bohr, a pioneer of atomic structure and quantum theory, was born on this day in 1885 in Copenhagen.","10-08":"Japan's Wood Day: put the kanji for 10 (十) and 8 (八) together and you get 木, \"tree\". The day was set in 1977.","10-09":"World Post Day, marking the founding of the Universal Postal Union in Bern, Switzerland, on this day in 1874.","10-10":"Eye Care Day in Japan: turn \"10 10\" on its side and it looks like a pair of eyebrows and eyes.","10-11":"On this day in 1968, Apollo 7 lifted off — the first Apollo mission to carry astronauts into space.","10-12":"Tenor Luciano Pavarotti, nicknamed the \"King of the High Cs\", was born on this day in 1935 in Modena, Italy.","10-13":"Sweet Potato Day in Japan: sweet potatoes were nicknamed \"13 ri\" — \"tastier than chestnuts (9 ri) by 4 ri\". Kawagoe fans set it up in 1987.","10-14":"Railway Day in Japan: the country's first railway opened between Shimbashi and Yokohama on this day in 1872. The trip took 53 minutes.","10-15":"Global Handwashing Day, held every year since 2008 to promote washing hands with soap.","10-16":"On this day in 1923, brothers Walt and Roy Disney founded the cartoon studio that became The Walt Disney Company.","10-17":"Okinawa Soba Day: on this day in 1978, the name \"Okinawa soba\" was officially approved for the island's wheat-noodle dish.","10-18":"On this day in 1958, \"Tennis for Two\", played on an oscilloscope, was shown at a U.S. lab — one of the very first video games.","10-19":"Astrophysicist Subrahmanyan Chandrasekhar, known for the \"Chandrasekhar limit\" on how stars die, was born on this day in 1910.","10-20":"On this day in 1973, the Sydney Opera House, with its famous sail-like roofs, officially opened.","10-21":"Japan's \"Day of Light\": on this day in 1879, Edison's incandescent lamp test lit up successfully.","10-22":"On this day in 1938, Chester Carlson made the first xerographic copy — \"10-22-38 ASTORIA\". The photocopier was born.","10-23":"Today is Mole Day, celebrated by chemists from 6:02 to 6:02 on 10/23 — a nod to Avogadro's number, 6.02×10²³.","10-24":"United Nations Day: the UN Charter came into force on this day in 1945, officially founding the UN.","10-25":"Pablo Picasso was born on this day in 1881, in Málaga, Spain.","10-26":"On this day in 1825, America's Erie Canal opened, linking the Great Lakes to the Hudson River and the Atlantic.","10-27":"Today is Teddy Bear Day: Theodore \"Teddy\" Roosevelt, who gave the bear its name, was born on this day in 1858.","10-28":"The Statue of Liberty, a gift from France to the United States, was dedicated in New York on this day in 1886.","10-29":"On this day in 1969, ARPANET — the internet's ancestor — sent its first message. It was meant to be \"LOGIN\", but only \"LO\" got through.","10-30":"Today is First Love Day in Japan: on this day in 1896, Shimazaki Tōson published his poem \"First Love\" in the magazine Bungakukai.","10-31":"Happy Halloween! The first jack-o'-lanterns, in Ireland and Britain, were carved from turnips, not pumpkins.","11-01":"In Japan it's Dog Day: 1-1-1 read as \"one, one, one\" sounds like \"wan wan wan\", the Japanese \"woof woof woof\". Set up in 1987.","11-02":"On this day in 1936, the BBC began the world's first regular high-definition TV service from Alexandra Palace in London.","11-03":"On this day in 1928, Osamu Tezuka, the \"god of manga\" and creator of Astro Boy, was born in Toyonaka, Osaka.","11-04":"On this day in 1922, Howard Carter found the first step leading down to Tutankhamun's tomb in Egypt.","11-05":"Guy Fawkes Night in Britain: bonfires and fireworks recall the foiled Gunpowder Plot of 1605.","11-06":"James Naismith, who invented basketball, was born on this day in 1861.","11-07":"On this day in 1867, Marie Curie was born in Warsaw. She won Nobel Prizes in both physics and chemistry.","11-08":"On this day in 1895, Wilhelm Röntgen discovered a mysterious new kind of ray in Germany. He called it the X-ray.","11-09":"On this day in 1934, astronomer Carl Sagan was born in Brooklyn, New York. His series Cosmos brought the universe to millions.","11-10":"On this day in 1969, Sesame Street aired for the first time on American public television.","11-11":"Today is Pocky & Pretz Day in Japan: Glico chose 11/11 in 1999 because the four 1s look like the snack sticks.","11-12":"On this day in 1840, sculptor Auguste Rodin, creator of The Thinker, was born in Paris.","11-13":"On this day in 1850, Robert Louis Stevenson, author of Treasure Island, was born in Edinburgh, Scotland.","11-14":"On this day in 1840, painter Claude Monet was born in Paris. His Impression, Sunrise gave Impressionism its name.","11-15":"Today is Shichi-Go-San in Japan, celebrating children aged 3, 5 and 7 — often with long, thin chitose-ame candy for a long life.","11-16":"On this day in 1945, the UNESCO Constitution was signed in London, founding the UN agency for education, science and culture.","11-17":"On this day in 1869, the Suez Canal opened in Egypt, linking the Mediterranean and the Red Sea — no more sailing around Africa.","11-18":"On this day in 1928, Steamboat Willie premiered in New York — the date Disney counts as Mickey Mouse's birthday.","11-19":"On this day in 1711, Russian scientist Mikhail Lomonosov was born. He helped found Moscow University.","11-20":"On this day in 1889, astronomer Edwin Hubble was born. He showed the universe is expanding, and a space telescope bears his name.","11-21":"On this day in 1783, two men flew freely over Paris in a Montgolfier hot-air balloon — the first human flight.","11-22":"Today is Good Couples Day in Japan — 11/22 can be read \"ii fūfu\", \"good married couple\". It was proposed in 1988.","11-23":"On this day in 1963, the BBC aired the first episode of Doctor Who, one of the longest-running sci-fi shows ever.","11-24":"On this day in 1859, Charles Darwin's On the Origin of Species was published, setting out evolution by natural selection.","11-25":"On this day in 1844, Karl Benz was born in Germany. He built one of the first practical petrol-powered cars.","11-26":"On this day in 1922, Charles M. Schulz, creator of Peanuts — Charlie Brown and Snoopy — was born in Minneapolis.","11-27":"On this day in 1895, Alfred Nobel signed his last will in Paris, leaving his fortune to create the Nobel Prizes.","11-28":"On this day in 1964, NASA launched Mariner 4. The next year it sent back the first close-up photos of Mars.","11-29":"On this day in 1972, Atari released Pong, the simple table-tennis arcade game that became a huge hit.","11-30":"On this day in 1835, Mark Twain, author of Tom Sawyer, was born in Missouri — the year Halley's Comet came by.","12-01":"Today is Movie Day in Japan, marking the first public showing of moving pictures — Edison's Kinetoscope — in Kobe in 1896.","12-02":"On this day in 1990, TV journalist Toyohiro Akiyama flew to space on a Soyuz, becoming the first Japanese person in space.","12-03":"On this day in 1992, the world's first SMS text message was sent in the UK. It said \"Merry Christmas\".","12-04":"On this day in 1791, The Observer was first published in London. It is the world's oldest Sunday newspaper.","12-05":"On this day in 1901, Walt Disney was born in Chicago. He gave the world Mickey Mouse and Disneyland.","12-06":"On this day in 1877, Thomas Edison recorded \"Mary Had a Little Lamb\" on his new phonograph — and played it back.","12-07":"Today is International Civil Aviation Day, marking the Chicago Convention signed on this day in 1944 — the basis of global air travel rules.","12-08":"On this day in 1865, Finnish composer Jean Sibelius, famous for Finlandia, was born in Hämeenlinna.","12-09":"On this day in 1968, Douglas Engelbart gave the \"Mother of All Demos\", showing off the computer mouse and hypertext.","12-10":"On this day in 1815, Ada Lovelace was born in London. Her notes on Babbage's Analytical Engine make her the \"first programmer\".","12-11":"Today is the UN's International Mountain Day, held since 2003 to celebrate mountains and the people who live among them.","12-12":"On this day in 1901, Guglielmo Marconi picked up the first radio signal sent across the Atlantic — the Morse letter \"S\".","12-13":"Today is Shōgatsu Koto-hajime in Japan, the traditional day to start getting ready for New Year — beginning with a big soot-sweeping clean.","12-14":"On this day in 1911, Norwegian explorer Roald Amundsen and his team became the first people to reach the South Pole.","12-15":"On this day in 1979, two journalists in Montreal came up with the trivia board game Trivial Pursuit.","12-16":"On this day in 1890, Japan's first public telephone service started between Tokyo and Yokohama.","12-17":"On this day in 1903, the Wright brothers made the first powered airplane flight: 12 seconds and about 37 m.","12-18":"On this day in 1879, painter Paul Klee was born near Bern, Switzerland. His colors and lines often feel like music.","12-19":"On this day in 1843, Charles Dickens published A Christmas Carol, the story of miserly Ebenezer Scrooge.","12-20":"On this day in 1914, Tokyo Station opened for service. Its red-brick Marunouchi building was designed by Tatsuno Kingo.","12-21":"On this day in 1913, the world's first crossword puzzle, by Arthur Wynne, appeared in the New York World newspaper.","12-22":"On this day in 1887, Indian mathematical genius Srinivasa Ramanujan was born. India celebrates it as National Mathematics Day.","12-23":"On this day in 1947, the transistor was first demonstrated at Bell Labs — the starting point of modern electronics.","12-24":"On this day in 1818, \"Silent Night\" was sung for the first time in Oberndorf, Austria — accompanied by a guitar.","12-25":"On this day in 1642 (by the calendar England used then), Isaac Newton was born. He described universal gravitation.","12-26":"On this day in 1791, Charles Babbage, the \"father of the computer\" who designed the gear-driven Difference Engine, was born in London.","12-27":"On this day in 1571, astronomer Johannes Kepler was born in Weil der Stadt, Germany. He discovered the laws of planetary motion.","12-28":"On this day in 1895, the Lumière brothers held a paid film screening at the Grand Café in Paris — often called the birth of cinema.","12-29":"On this day in 1800, Charles Goodyear was born. He invented vulcanization, using sulfur to make rubber tough and useful.","12-30":"On this day in 1927, Asia's first subway opened in Tokyo, running 2.2 km between Ueno and Asakusa.","12-31":"It's New Year's Eve! Across Japan, temple bells ring 108 times — joya no kane — to see out the old year."}, "On this day", {"new":"New game","3d":"3D","online":"Online","rules":"Rules"});
